(6459124, 958350, 125275, '<td valign="top">Ha, saw your other image in the free study. That is, assuming someone didn''t have an extremely similar idea! This is a great execution of this idea. The texture of the paper is visible where it needs to be, the blade is a nice cool grey (definitely couldn''t have done the shark fin here), and the shadows and lighting are soft, almost subtle. Nicely done. (and in case I don''t comment and the image in the FS is yours, that one is cool too!)</td>', 'Ha, saw your other image in the free study. That is, assuming someone didn''t have an extremely similar idea! This is a great execution of this idea. The texture of the paper is visible where it needs to be, the blade is a nice cool grey (definitely couldn''t have done the shark fin here), and the shadows and lighting are soft, almost subtle. Nicely done. (and in case I don''t comment and the image in the FS is yours, that one is cool too!)', '2011-07-02 19:58:44.000000', NULL, 1),
